## Implementation

**1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourNamespace.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // Falls through to default handler (returns 500, no sensitive details)

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title = title,
            Detail = title,
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

// ... after building the app:

app.UseExceptionHandler();  // Invokes IExceptionHandler chain
app.UseStatusCodePages();   // Converts bare status codes to Problem Details
```

## How it works

- `AddProblemDetails()` configures the default handler to return RFC 7807 JSON for unhandled exceptions (500) **without** leaking exception messages or stack traces.
- Your custom `IExceptionHandler` intercepts known exceptions and maps them to appropriate status codes. Returning `false` for unknown exceptions delegates to the built-in handler.
- `UseStatusCodePages()` ensures non-exception error responses (e.g., middleware returning 404) also use Problem Details format.

No try-catch needed in endpoints — the middleware pipeline handles everything globally.
